Like most 6-year-olds, Edmund Picciuto likes to sing, toys and, of course, his mother.
But, unlike most other peers, Edmund has microcephaly, or congenital small-headedness due to the genetic disorder of his mother Elizabeth Picciuto, of which, while he was pregnant, he was unaware.
