For the first time, Bulgaria Announces Inflamination for Eight Months
According to national statistics, Bulgaria's monthly inflation rate was 1% in July.
That's the highest value for many years (since June 2012) and the first time it's rising to more than zero since October of last year, when the country reported a 0.2 per cent positive inflation.
CPI-measured average annual inflation over the last 12 months (August-July 2015 to July 2016) compared to previous 12 months (August 2014 to July 2015) was -0.8%.
Compared to June 2016, the Consumer Price Indicative Index in July 2016 stood at 101.0%, i.e. monthly inflation rate of 1.0 per cent.
Inflation rate since the beginning of the year (priced per cent of July 2016 compared to December 2015 per cent) has been -0.2 per cent, compared to July 2016.
Compared to the previous month in July 2016, the prices of the following categories of consumer goods were observed: food and non-alcoholic drinks (1.7%), vehicles (1.8%), recreation and culture (6.3%), rehesers and hotels (1.2%), other goods and services (0.3%).
Prices went down in clothing and footwear (2.2%), furnishings, household appliances and fixed-on-term maintenance (0.5%), and health (0.1%).
Prices for the following product groups remained at the same level as the previous month: alcoholic beverages and cigarettes, dwellings, water, electricity, gas and other fuels, communications and education.
Snapchat's anime effect is criticised as an Asian caricature
Snapchat says it's an anime inspired by that filter, but some observers think it's racist.
