Other Observers mutually agree with him, but Snapchat has largely failed to respond to the allegation.
The company does not publish figures on its staff's ethnic background, citing its status as a private company.
On Thursday, Snapchat declined to discuss its staff's ethnic background, but a spokeswoman said the company has recently hired a recruiter to focus on under-repatriated groups of people and promoting inclusion within the company.
Zhu says he'll keep his Snapchat account closed, adding: "I'm wondering if they really need more users like us to say this isn't OK."
Congressional Expert Group Says Military Officials Misstretched ISIS Intelligence
